## Antigravity specifics

- **Skills and agents** — the rolepod skills ship inside the plugin
  (`~/.gemini/config/plugins/rolepod/skills/`) and show as slash commands
  (e.g. `/write-spec`); 15 specialists ship as plugin subagents, each
  carrying its own protocol. agy does not dispatch by description: spawn
  the specialist a skill names, by its name.
- **Tier classes** — cheap / balanced / strong are CLASSES, never model
  names; agy picks models, so request by class: sweep / read = the fast
  class, build / verify = the pro class, the ONE judge or security reviewer
  = the strongest available — never the whole fan-out; cannot classify →
  balanced, and say so.
- **Enforcement** — one hook denies: `PreToolUse` on `run_command` blocks a
  commit with `docs/rolepod/` staged. agy has no context-injection channel,
  so this file is the only always-on text. Every other rule is
  skill-enforced — never report it as mechanically enforced.
